I've never quite understood the idea of putting marshmallows on sweet potatoes, but since I'm cooking my way through the World of Warcraft cookbook, I was bound to come across this particular Pilgrim’s Bounty recipe eventually.

The sweet potatoes are baked with butter, honey, brown sugar and the cookbook's Autumnal Herbs spice blend. Apparently, that isn't quite sweet enough, so the whole thing gets topped with a marshmallow meringue made with egg whites, maple syrup and marshmallow fluff.

I suspect I boiled my sweet potatoes a little too long, and my meringue probably could have done with slightly less time in the oven as well. At least the little meringue clouds managed to hold their shape.

The cookbook recommends serving these alongside Slow-Roasted Turkey, and I’m still trying to wrap my head around having something this sweet as part of the main course rather than dessert. But I suppose Pilgrim’s Bounty isn't the time to worry about how much sugar goes into a vegetable side dish.
